A branched amino tetrasaccharide consisting of a linear trisaccharide derivative of α-L-fucose, N-acetyl-β-D-glucosamine and (at the reducing end) α-D-mannose residues linked sequentially (1→4) and (1→2), to the N-acetyl-β-D-glucosamine residue of which is also linked (1→3) a β-D-galactose residue.

